18. Yea, all things which come of the earth, in the season thereof, are
made for the benefit and the use of man, both to please the eye and to
gladden the heart;
19. Yea, for food and for raiment, for taste and for smell, to strengthen
the body and to enliven the soul.
20. And it pleaseth God that he hath given all these things unto man;
for unto this end were they made to be used, with judgment, not to excess,
neither by extortion.
